lesson: `
<p>A sequence is an ordered list of numbers. A series is the sum of terms of a sequence.</p>

<p>An arithmetic sequence has a common difference.</p>

<div class="formula">
T<sub>n</sub> = a + (n-1)d
</div>

<p>The sum of the first n terms is:</p>

<div class="formula">
S<sub>n</sub> = n/2 [2a+(n-1)d]
</div>

<p>A geometric sequence has a common ratio.</p>
`,

example: `
<p><b>Example 1:</b> Find the 10th term of 3,7,11,15,...</p>
<p>a=3, d=4.</p>
<p>T₁₀=3+9(4)=<b>39</b>.</p>

<p><b>Example 2:</b> Find the sum of the first 10 terms.</p>
<p>S₁₀=10/2[6+36]=<b>210</b>.</p>
`,

