lesson: `
<p>Modular arithmetic deals with remainders after division.</p>

<div class="formula">
a ≡ b (mod n)
</div>

<p>This means that a and b leave the same remainder when divided by n.</p>

<p>For example, 17 ≡ 5 (mod 12), because both leave remainder 5.</p>

<p>Modular arithmetic is useful in clock calculations, calendars and computer science.</p>
`,

