<p>The order of a matrix is written as m × n, where m is the number of rows and n is the number of columns.</p>

<p>A matrix with two rows and three columns is a 2 × 3 matrix.</p>

<p>Matrices can be added or subtracted when they have the same order.</p>

<p>Matrix multiplication follows specific rules and is different from ordinary multiplication of corresponding entries.</p>
`,

example: `
